# Kernel patches are applied with plain `git apply` against byte-exact files
# inside dsh-runtime/node_modules, so the patch files must be checked out
# exactly as committed (LF) on every platform.
#
# Without this, Git for Windows (core.autocrlf=true by default) rewrites the
# patch file to CRLF in the working tree while the target node_modules file
# stays LF, and `git apply` then fails with:
#   error: patch failed: ...:395
#   error: ...: patch does not apply
# (Windows CI run 34960957498 / 35007381714 failed exactly this way.)
scripts/dsh-kernel-patches/*.patch -text
